<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Storia d'Italia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1537–1540</span> · Also known as History of Italy (Guicciardini)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Storia d'Italia, or History of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, is a historical work by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-guicciardini">Francesco Guicciardini</a>, written in the last years of his life and published after his death, from 1561. Covering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a> from 1490 to 1534, it treats Italy as a whole and explains events through the calculations of rulers and the balance of power. It was widely translated and is a landmark of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> historiography.</p></div>
